A74 P5 - cfMesh's 2-D mesher against the lane's own O-mesh.
Linux build container, OpenFOAM v2606 (openfoam.com), 2026-09-08.
Every mesh single-threaded (OMP_NUM_THREADS=1). NACA 0012, chord 1.0 m,
30 m/s, alpha 4 deg, kOmegaSST, slab 0.1 m thick, Aref = chord x thickness.

== p5-closed-surface.py: the 3-D idiom, four ways ==
cell 1.0 slab 0.1   (the first try)    rc=1 in   0.6 s   --> FOAM FATAL ERROR: (openfoam-2606)
cell 0.999 slab 0.1  (not a divisor)   rc=1 in   0.4 s   --> FOAM FATAL ERROR: (openfoam-2606)
cell 0.1  slab 0.1   (cell = slab)     rc=1 in   0.9 s   --> FOAM FATAL ERROR: (openfoam-2606)
cell 0.999 slab 1.0  (slab = cell)     rc=1 in   0.4 s   --> FOAM FATAL ERROR: (openfoam-2606)
  (all four: 'There are no cells in the mesh!', in under a second)

== p5-ribbon-surface.py: the surface OPEN in z ==
ribbon box + ribbon airfoil    rc=0   1.6 s  cells 8572  skew 1.3762784  failed 2  patches [('farfield', 'empty'), ('airfoil', 'empty'), ('bottomEmptyFaces', 'empty'), ('topEmptyFaces', 'empty')]
ribbon box + capped airfoil    rc=0   1.7 s  cells 8572  skew 0.83798945  failed 2  patches [('farfield', 'empty'), ('airfoil', 'empty'), ('bottomEmptyFaces', 'empty'), ('topEmptyFaces', 'empty')]

== patch types cfMesh wrote, and after the caller fixed them ==
  as written: farfield empty | airfoil empty | bottomEmptyFaces empty | topEmptyFaces empty
  checkMesh:  ***Total number of faces on empty patches is not divisible by the
              number of cells in the mesh. Hence this mesh is not 1D or 2D.
  rewritten:  farfield patch | airfoil wall | bottomEmptyFaces empty | topEmptyFaces empty
  checkMesh:  Mesh OK.  cells 8572  skew 0.83798945  aspect 5.7560163

